<title>USA: TABLE-Medical Assurance Inc Q2 shr rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Medical Assurance Inc Q2 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				 Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					    June 30,	  June 30,</p>
<p>					   1997    1996    1997    1996</p>
<p> Total revenues		    38,692  28,895  77,163  59,154</p>
<p>Expenses</p>
<p>Net losses and loss</p>
<p>   adjustment expenses	   19,207  13,310  39,444  29,342</p>
<p>Underwriting, acquisition</p>
<p>   and insurance expense	  8,052   5,173  15,192  10,907</p>
<p> Total expenses		    27,259  18,483  54,636  40,249</p>
<p> NET INCOME			   8,781   7,661  17,195  14,517</p>
<p>Earnings per share</p>
<p>  Net income			   0.86    0.77    1.68    1.46</p>
<p>  Operating earnings		 0.87    0.74    1.67    1.43</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>  common shares outstanding    10,238   9,931  10,256   9,931</p>
<p>Note: Results for 1997 include the operations of MOMED Holding Co, the parent company of Missouri Medical Insurance Co, which was acquired by Medical Assurance in December 1996.</p>
<p>The company said $3.3 million of its revenue increase was attributable to MOMED.</p>
</text>
